# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 5.
title: Open 2NT with 21
id: L02-07
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.2
student: S
board: 7
dealer: S
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  K92    J852   Q74    Q93
  E  T83    T4     KT8632 A5
  S  AQJ6   KQ3    AJ     KJT8
  W  754    A976   95     7642

auction:
  S 2NT*   = 21-22 points, balanced
     key: 21 HCP and balanced: open 2NT.
     not 1NT: Did you count 21? That's too strong for 1NT, which shows 15-17.
     not 1C: Did you count 21? A balanced 21-22 opens 2NT.
     not 1S: Did you count 21? A balanced 21-22 opens 2NT.
     not 2C: Did you count 21? A two-bid in a suit needs 22 and a five-card suit.
     not 3NT: Did you count 21? 3NT shows 23-25.
     not *: Did you count 21? A balanced 21-22 opens 2NT.
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = 4+ points: game
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Partner knows you have 21-22, so she knows your side has 25+. Pass.
     not *: Partner knew your range and chose game. Is there anything left to say?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  2NT describes your hand in one bid: 21-22 points, balanced. Partner
  needs only 4 points to know your side has 25, so with 8 she bids game.
  You are declarer, because you bid no-trump first, and so West will lead
  to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W H6  N H2  E HT  S HK
  2   S CT  W C2  N C3  E CA
      note: The plan: drive out the ♣A, and lead toward the ♦J for a second diamond trick: if East has the king, the jack wins.
  3   E H4  S H3  W H9  N HJ
      note: East returns partner's suit.
  4   N D4  E D2  S DJ  W D5
      note: A diamond from dummy toward your ♦AJ. If East has the king, your jack wins.
  5   S C8  W C4  N CQ  E C5
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q.
  6   N C9  E D3  S CK  W C6
      note: Back to your ♣K.
  7   S CJ  W C7  N S2  E D6
      note: Your last club is a winner.
  8   S DA  W D9  N D7  E D8
      note: Cash the ♦A.
  9   S S6  W S4  N SK  E S3
      note: A spade to dummy's king.
  10  N S9  E S8  S SJ  W S5
      note: Back to your spades.
  11  S SQ  W S7  N H5  E ST
      note: Keep going.
  12  S SA  W H7  N H8  E DT
      note: The last spade.
  13  S HQ  W HA  N DQ  E DK
      note: West's ♥A takes the last trick. 11 tricks: 3NT made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  The plan: drive out the ♣A, and lead toward the ♦J for a second
  diamond trick. It works when East has the king, as here.

  3NT made with two overtricks. Partner had 8 points, and with your 21
  that made 29: plenty for game.
